      "Text": "libical security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libical is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Libical is an open source implementation of the IETF\u0026apos;s iCalendar calendaring and scheduling protocols (RFC 2445, 2446, and 2447). It parses iCal components and provides a C API for manipulating the component properties, parameters, and subcomponents.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nlibical through 4.0.6 contains a heap-based out-of-bounds read in icalvalue_decode_ical_string() in src/libical/icalvalue.c when decoding input ending in a backslash. Attackers can supply escaped iCalendar text with a trailing backslash, causing the loop to read past the terminator and crash the application or leak adjacent heap memory.(CVE-2026-111269)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libical is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of medium. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Medium",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "libical",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
